 "text": "Hey! How's everything with you? Lightly packed sandwiches, cake, bananas, apple cuts into bite sized pieces, that kind of thing. Sandwiches are the easiest, you can stop at a cafe on the way. Park at base and take a short walk, an hour each way gives you time to stop and rest without outating night. A small box of chocolates or a bag of sweets would last all day and is worth it after a long hike. If you think you might stop at a cafe, avoid them until you' at or near the spot. Sticks can get stuck and a full cup of coffee can get cold.",
